  "response_text": "If the thread function didn\u2019t loop and instead returned after printing once, the CPU would attempt to pop the return address from the stack and jump to it using the Link Register (LR). However, as threads are usually designed to run indefinitely using an infinite loop or similar means, returning from the thread would cause the CPU to jump to an invalid memory location stored in LR or on the stack, leading to a hard fault. The address stored in LR is usually invalid because threads are not expected to return. The hard fault occurs because the processor tries to execute code from an invalid or protected memory region.\\n",
